{"kind":"request","text":"S4: hosted MCP findings, before any Worker opens hosted MCP\n\nFrom the attack-surface review of 10 November 2026 (planner request\n79daff0f, at main 7177b87b). Read its sections 3.1 to 3.5 and the two\nhosted MCP items of 1.7. Every live Worker answers 404 on /mcp today. I\nset `MCP_ENABLED` on no Worker until this head lands.\n\nOne head, with checker review.\n\n1. Finding 3.1. A member cannot spend a room's control budget for good.\n   The read-only control `connections` stores no row, or the registry\n   releases the row after its `notAfter` window. Control routes have a\n   window for each key. The consent page's own calls spend nothing that\n   stays spent.\n2. Finding 3.2. GET /oauth/authorize/context has an address window, and\n   an invalid client document is cached as invalid for a short time.\n3. Finding 3.3. The role-subset rule holds at each use: bearer rotation,\n   create, refresh and access standing. An agent whose role an admin\n   widens past its controller's role gains no action from the change.\n4. Finding 3.4. A card's script cannot call a write tool. Read the\n   current MCP Apps specification for the visibility field before you\n   choose the form, and cite the section in the note.\n5. Finding 3.5. A refused grant leaves no client mapping. `credential`\n   returns its secret outside `structuredContent`.\n6. Finding 1.7. `grant` resolves the OAuth client after the signature\n   check. The control route registers no membership ID from an\n   unverified header.\n\nWitness. One test for each item that fails at 7177b87b. For item 1: more\n`connections` calls than the budget holds, then a `create` that still\nsucceeds.\n\nDocuments. The head corrects docs/hosted-mcp.md (lines 184 and 293 at\n7177b87b), and the budget paragraph of\nnotes/2026-10-13-hosted-mcp-endpoint.md (lines 510 to 526).\n\nOrder. After OPS-2 in the gate order, or after identifiers (c+d) if the\nhead collides with it in packages/mcp. You say which. It lands before\nthe O4 live window.","body":{"conditions":"One head with checker review closes findings 3.1 to 3.5 and the two hosted MCP items of 1.7 of review 79daff0f, each with a test that fails at 7177b87b. It lands before any Worker opens hosted MCP.","target_head":"7177b87be03ced9e2ddae2a5ebfcdfffcc1fda62","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}